{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"UNBLOCKED and resumed. Filed 3 unparented bugs for general rebar problems: unquieting-godsent-mammal (P1, LLM ops hang for hours despite REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT), bediasite-bilineate-stoat (P2, close gate demands a file_impact edit that then stales the attestation), perkish-balsamic-pupfish (P2, superseded tickets cannot be closed - review cannot pass BECAUSE the work is already done). S3, S6 closed cleanly. S4 needed a fast-forward of the worktree to merged origin/main (its attestation was pinned to a pre-merge SHA and read stale-code) then re-reviewed PASS+signed and closed, unblocking S5 and S7. S5 force-closed as superseded with a detailed reason citing perkish-balsamic-pupfish - no verification bypassed, the work landed and was verified under S4; the missing attestation is the intended audit signal. S7 (final story): review PASS first try, claimed, oracle RED-first, edge held out, implementer 1 attempt. Verified the critical compatibility line at completion_verifier.md:95 directly against origin/main (the agent's report quoted it with a typo) - intact and unmodified. Held-out validation 9 passed. Mutation teeth: regressing the READER to canonical-only kills the historical-verdict test; stripping the legacy-tag sentence kills the recognition test - the two ways this could silently break 827 tickets are both caught. lint clean, mypy 598 files, 65 passed. Pushed as change 1958."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787254416763323001,"uuid":"aefcdeee-3d8d-4bc2-b8d4-f98865c74491"}